-      CONTEXT
-      Recent work on protocol-level identifiability (arXiv:2608.13326) and sampling-verification danger (arXiv:2608.17956) shows that local accuracy can be precise while the observation support does not identify the claimed intervention effect. V557 needs a reusable zero-inference preflight before held causal selection. It also needs the existing task-scoped receipt contract to cover queue, load, execution, exact verification, and artifact phases. Work at {project_root}. The planning date is {date}.
