-      0. Record repository state, exact runtime dependencies, existing receipt schema hash, policy-class fixture hash, and available exact reducers.
-      1. Add REQ-* and SCENARIO-* entries for protocol identifiability and receipt conformance. Write focused tests first.
-      2. Implement a finite deterministic API that groups policies by their outcomes on observation support and detects cross-estimand collisions.
-      3. Emit a constructive pair of policies for every collision. Preserve the differing target effect and the identical observed outcomes.
-      4. Synthesize a minimum identifying support for the frozen held-selection policy class. Verify it by exhaustive enumeration.
-      5. Include positive controls, leave-one-support-out collisions, duplicated observations, empty support, constant estimand, and changed-policy-class attacks.
-      6. Validate queue_wait, model_load_or_fixture_load, execution, exact_verification, and artifact_write receipt phases with monotonic times, hashes, PIDs, exit status, and CPU fallback state.
-      7. Emit one row per policy pair, support condition, attack, and receipt phase. Recompute all aggregates from rows.
-      8. Run focused tests, 100% task-module coverage, spec coverage, row lint, adversarial verification, and applicable E2E checks. Inspect git status after tests.
-      9. Set protocol_identifying_score=1.0 only when the declared support has no cross-estimand collision, every required receipt phase is conformant, and every non-identifying control yields a witness.
